# Project One Move-Between-Rooms Pseudocode
#
# Graded checkpoint: Module Five Project One
# Later use: conceptual support for M6; movement design for M7
#
# Review the course-provided movement flowchart before completing this file.
# Write pseudocode, not Python code. Use clear indentation and course-appropriate
# keywords such as INPUT, OUTPUT, IF, ELSE, WHILE, SET, or similar terms.

SET current_room TO "Study Room"


SET game_is_running TO TRUE

WHILE game_is_running
    OUTPUT "Which direction would you like to move? North, South, East, or West?"
    INPUT movement_command

    IF movement_command leads to a connected room from current_room THEN 
        SET current_room TO the room connected in movement_command direction
        OUTPUT "You move " + movement_command
        OUTPUT "You are now in " + current_room

    ELSE
        OUTPUT "Invalid direction. Please try again."
    END IF
    IF player reaches the required ending THEN
        SET game_is_running TO FALSE
    END IF
END WHILE





